$T$ is the point of contact where tangent $TP$ touches the circle, centre $O$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (T) at (0,2.2);
\coordinate (P) at (3.142,2.2);
\draw (O) circle (2.2);
\fill (O) circle (1.5pt);
\node[below left] at (O) {$O$};
\draw (O) -- (T) -- (P) -- (O);
\node[above left] at (T) {$T$};
\node[right] at (P) {$P$};
\coordinate (ta) at ($(T)!0.3cm!(O)$);
\coordinate (tp) at ($(T)!0.3cm!(P)$);
\draw (ta) -- ($(ta)+(tp)-(T)$) -- (tp);
\pic[draw, "$55^{\circ}$", angle radius=0.6cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle=P--O--T};
\pic[draw, "$x$", angle radius=0.5cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle=T--P--O};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the value of $x$.

